# Option A — project root: copy this file to  .env.local.properties  (gitignored)
# Option B — IntelliJ / Maven: put the same line in  src/main/resources/application-local.properties
#            (also gitignored). No SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE needed — it is imported automatically.
#
# --- MongoDB Atlas (mongodb+srv) ---
# Paste the same connection string you use in MongoDB Compass:
#   Compass → your connection → "Copy connection string"
# Special characters in the password must be URL-encoded (e.g. @ → %40)
#
# If the app logs SSLException / "internal_error" / TLS alert 80 to *.mongodb.net:27017, the JVM
# usually is not at fault. Atlas → Network Access must allow this machine's *public* egress IP
# (VPN/office changes it). Try Compass on the same Mac; try Atlas IP 0.0.0.0/0 only for local dev.
# IntelliJ: if JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS sets javax.net.ssl.trustStore to a PKCS12, you can still try Atlas;
# this project defaults mongo.srv.trust-strategy=jdk-cacerts for mongodb+srv.
#
# --- Local Mongo (no Atlas) ---
# docker compose up -d mongo
# mongo_uri=mongodb://localhost:27017/openProject
#
#
# --- AI Data Agent (REQUIRED for /ai-agent) ---
# Domain-only LLM agent. Free local: Groq (no card) → https://console.groq.com/keys
# ai.agent.api-key=gsk_...
# ai.agent.base-url=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# ai.agent.model=llama-3.1-8b-instant
# Paid OpenAI alternative:
# ai.agent.api-key=sk-...
# ai.agent.base-url=https://api.openai.com/v1
# ai.agent.model=gpt-4o-mini
#
mongo_uri=mongodb+srv://USERNAME:PASSWORD@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/openProject
